david pittman was just 12 years old when  he was sexually abused by a youth  minister at his southern baptist church  in georgia he told no one you know this  is the person that's supposed to  represent god  and they're doing this so i i who am i  going to tell what what am i going to  tell them i'm a 12 year old who's never  been taught any of these things  the abuse continued for three years the  trauma and shame later led him to  addiction i wanted in just as much of it  as i could so i didn't have to think  about what had happened to me  and so for 20 years i'm abusing drugs my  life  spirals out of control with 14 million  members and 47 000 affiliated churches  the sbc is the largest protestant  denomination in the u.s and a powerful  force in conservative politics but  southern baptists are reeling from  revelations of widespread sexual abuse  of children by ministers and church  officials i think the report did rock  people to their core i mean mixture of  indignation grief for decades church  leaders made extensive efforts to cover  it all up last month an independent  third party report documented how the  southern baptist convention's executive  committee dismissed allegations of  sexual abuse ignored survivors and their  stories and focused instead on  protecting the organization's reputation  and sparing individual congregations  from legal liability  the sbc will consider a series of  reforms including a database of proven  and suspected offenders  predators try to remain anonymous i mean  that's what they do they try to stay in  the background we're going to put a  mechanism in place where as best we can  those people are recognized  and  communicated that they can't keep  hurting other folks the sex abuse task  force will also recommend a full apology  for survivors but the apology is only as  good as the action you know one of the  things that has been frustrating is to  survivors has been a lot of talk  without concrete change  pittman is skeptical i don't believe in  institutional change what i hope is that  there's  over time there is a continuum a  continuum of leadership  that is trying to help survivors if that  takes place then it is possible  for some  wholesale and long-term institutional  change a powerful church humbled forced  to confront the betrayal of its children  rob reynolds al jazeera anaheim  california
 

